{{also|Reverend|révérend}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|révérend}}, from {{der|en|fro|-}}, from {{der|en|la|-}} future passive participle {{m|la|reverendus||that is to be respected}}, from deponent verb {{m|la|revereor||I honor, revere}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛvɹənd/|/ˈɹɛvəɹənd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-reverend.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{head|en|adjective}}

# [[worthy]] of [[reverence]] or [[respect]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} a member of the [[Christian]] [[clergy]]

====Derived terms====
* '''Reverend Gentleman''' (referring to a [[clergyman]])
* [[Right Reverend]] (when referring to an [[Anglican]] [[bishop]])

